  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 102.59 Discharge",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 102.59 “Discharge” means the accidental or intentional release, spilling, leaking, pumping, pouring, emitting, emptying, or dumping of any solid waste or solid waste constituent, including leachate, into or on any air, land, or water.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; renumbered by #13357 (formerly Env-Sw 102.49); ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 102.47) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
